[0m[0m
Key implementation details:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mKDTree::build[0m — caches point coordinates, then recursively builds the tree by sorting points along alternating axes (x→y→z) and splitting at the median[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mKDTree::search[0m — converts a center point + apothem into a bounding box and delegates to the space search[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msearch_space_iter[0m — the core search entry point that initializes/resets the iterator, sets up the infinite initial domain, and kicks off recursive tree traversal[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mdo_search_kd[0m / [38;5;10mdo_explore_branch[0m / [38;5;10mcollect_all_leaves[0m — free functions implementing the recursive search: they split the domain along the current axis, prune branches that don't intersect the search space, and bulk-collect all leaves when a domain is fully enclosed[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mKDTreeIterator[0m — manages search results with [38;5;10mpush[0m, [38;5;10mget_next[0m, [38;5;10mreset[0m, [38;5;10mrewind[0m, and [38;5;10msort[0m[0m[0m
- Compare functions ([38;5;10mcompare_x/y/z/size_t[0m) — used for sorting points by axis and sorting iterator results[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The methods with [38;5;10m&KDTreeIterator[0m signatures ([38;5;10mreport_all_leaves[0m, [38;5;10mexplore_branch[0m, [38;5;10msearch_kd[0m) couldn't mutate the iterator, so the actual logic lives in free functions that take [38;5;10m&mut Vec<usize>[0m, with results pushed into the iterator afterward. No [38;5;10munsafe[0m code was needed.[0m[0m[38;5;12m[1m✓ Created checkpoint 1

